twisted.conch.endpoints.SSHCommandClientEndpoint now supports the hostkeys-00@openssh.com host-key update extension. When the current host key is already trusted, additional host keys advertised by the server are learned only after a valid proof of possession is verified, and they are saved to the known hosts file so rotated host keys can authenticate subsequent connections. Invalid proofs, unsupported key algorithms, and save failures leave the existing known-hosts records unchanged.
